    {
      "id": "BZZwESgewGWEaNHhG7mIf",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -7122.0053341307785,
      "y": 2707.589690392166,
      "width": 1691.4189453125,
      "height": 750,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aA",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 637661919,
      "version": 2245,
      "versionNonce": 1569855,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783690348623,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "How to avoid showing repeat profiles?\n- User don't want to see repeat profiles, it could annoy them\n\nBad Solution : DB Query + Contains Check\n- In feed builder service do contains check to filter our users who have been swiped before\n- we get all the swiped-on profiles and remove them from current feed.\n\nProblems : not all swiping data might've landed in all replicas by the time feed is being generated, meaning risk of missing swipes and risk of re-showing\n- if extensive swipe history, this way is very computation expensive.\n\n\n\nGreat Solution : Cache + DB Query + Contains Check\n- We have client store its recent swipe data (k most recent swipes), allowing client to filter out profiles that might be suggested in feed but already been swiped on by user\n- Assumption is user is only using this app on one device\n- Problem could be with users with extensive swipe histories and large user Id contains checks gets slower with more swipe data\n\n\n\n\nGreat Solution : Cache + Contains Check + Bloom Filter\n- Built on top of our previous approach, for user with large swipe history consider storing a bloom filter.\n- If swipe history exceeded certain size(a value making contains costly), build and cache a bloom filter.\n- we can get false positives, meaning we assume a user swiped on a profile but they didn't swipe on, but zero false negatives\n- meaning we'll never say user have not swiped on a profile they actually did swipe on.\n- meaning we avoid re-showing of profiles but there's a small nos of profile we never show to the user\n- Bloom filters are tunable based on how much space they take \n\nProblem : managing bloom filter cache is challenging, needs to be updated and recoverd if it goes down, easy to re-create with swipe data but would be expensive at scale.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "How to avoid showing repeat profiles?\n- User don't want to see repeat profiles, it could annoy them\n\nBad Solution : DB Query + Contains Check\n- In feed builder service do contains check to filter our users who have been swiped before\n- we get all the swiped-on profiles and remove them from current feed.\n\nProblems : not all swiping data might've landed in all replicas by the time feed is being generated, meaning risk of missing swipes and risk of re-showing\n- if extensive swipe history, this way is very computation expensive.\n\n\n\nGreat Solution : Cache + DB Query + Contains Check\n- We have client store its recent swipe data (k most recent swipes), allowing client to filter out profiles that might be suggested in feed but already been swiped on by user\n- Assumption is user is only using this app on one device\n- Problem could be with users with extensive swipe histories and large user Id contains checks gets slower with more swipe data\n\n\n\n\nGreat Solution : Cache + Contains Check + Bloom Filter\n- Built on top of our previous approach, for user with large swipe history consider storing a bloom filter.\n- If swipe history exceeded certain size(a value making contains costly), build and cache a bloom filter.\n- we can get false positives, meaning we assume a user swiped on a profile but they didn't swipe on, but zero false negatives\n- meaning we'll never say user have not swiped on a profile they actually did swipe on.\n- meaning we avoid re-showing of profiles but there's a small nos of profile we never show to the user\n- Bloom filters are tunable based on how much space they take \n\nProblem : managing bloom filter cache is challenging, needs to be updated and recoverd if it goes down, easy to re-create with swipe data but would be expensive at scale.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
